<title>ITALY: Italy cabinet approves end-year fiscal package.</title>
<headline>Italy cabinet approves end-year fiscal package.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian cabinet has approved a package of end-year fiscal measures, forming the last part of the 1997 austerity budget, government sources said.</p>
<p>The cabinet began discussing the measures at 1000 GMT on Monday. The package had been meant to raise some 4.3 trillion lire next year out of the total budget worth 62.5 trillion lire.</p>
<p>The value of the package approved was not immediately known.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +392 66129589</p>
